    "description": {
      "value": "<p>An upgraded shotgun with a higher range and larger magazine.</p><p>Ammo Type: Shells</p><p>Reload: 10 shots</p><p>Damage: 2d6 piercing (2d8 scatter)</p><p>Range: 80/320 ft</p><p><strong>Reload:</strong> A reloadable weapon can be used to make a number of attacks before it must be reloaded. Reloading requires a free hand, and takes a bonus action or an action (character's choice).</p><p><strong>Strength 11:</strong> Any creature using this weapon has disadvantage on attack rolls with it if its Strength score is less than the value of the strength requirement. Furthermore, when making a ranged attack with this weapon, you may use your Strength modifier instead of your Dexterity modifier for attack rolls.</p><p><strong>Scatter:</strong> If you make an attack with a scatter weapon that is within half the weapon's normal range, you deal the damage value listed in parenthesis instead of the weapon's normal damage dice.</p>",
